ADVANCED CTEs:all three are same clause below
CTEs clause,
subquery factoring clause,
WITH clause
-if i have more than 1 sub queries in my query CTEs are used
-all sub queries are converted into common table expression(CTE) and treat then as table
------------------------
alias:population table as county
alias:cte table as cont
alias : cte_world table as word
---------------------
with cte_contint AS
(SELECT continent,SUM(total_population)AS cont_population FROM population GROUP BY continent)      
SELECT county.country,county.continent,county.total_population county.cont_population FROM population county
JOIN cte_contint cont
ON (county.continent=cont.continent)
JOIN cte_world world

using multiple CTEs:
---------------------
adding more than 1 cte to the query:
with cte_contint AS
(SELECT continent,SUM(total_population)AS cont_population FROM population GROUP BY continent)   ,
cte_world AS (SELECT SUM(total_population)AS world_population FROM population)
SELECT county.country,county.continent,county.total_population, county.cont_population,world.world_population
FROM population county
JOIN cte_contint cont
ON (county.continent=cont.continent)
JOIN cte_world world
